<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
      THIS COMMENT IS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT ON PURPOSE - a comment ABOVE the root breaks sf at
      source conversion with a misleading parent-xml error.

      Contract Executed WAS ADDED HERE (GATE-B2). The auto-create service projects four dates from
      the deal: Contract Executed, Earnest Money Due, Feasibility End and Closing Date. Three of
      those already had a value; Contract Executed did not.

      THIS VALUE MUST DEPLOY BEFORE ANY APEX THAT WRITES IT. The value set is restricted=true, and
      restricted picklists ARE enforced by Apex DML on this org - measured four separate times,
      including on LOI__c.Stage__c and Contract_Review__c.Negotiation_Status__c. Writing an absent
      value raises INVALID_OR_NULL_FOR_RESTRICTED_PICKLIST; it is not coerced and it is not a
      warning. Deploying the Apex first therefore produces a runtime failure that no compile and no
      dry run catches.

      APPENDED AT THE END, NOT INSERTED IN CHRONOLOGICAL POSITION. The existing order is already
      non-chronological (Closing Date is first), sorted is false, and no Path or record type reads
      this field, so ordering carries no behaviour here. Appending keeps the diff to one block and
      leaves the five existing values byte-identical.
    -->
    <fullName>Type__c</fullName>
    <description>Which deadline this critical date represents. Restricted, and paired with the parent Transaction it forms the idempotency key the auto-create service uses, so one deal carries at most one row per type and a re-run heals rather than duplicates. Contract Executed was added 2026-08-31 for the checklist rewrite - see the XML comment in this file for the deploy-order constraint that comes with it.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Which deadline this row represents. One row per type per deal; the projection service keeps the date pinned to the matching field on the deal.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Type</label>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Picklist</type>
    <valueSet>
        <restricted>true</restricted>
        <valueSetDefinition>
            <sorted>false</sorted>
            <value>
                <fullName>Closing Date</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Closing Date</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Feasibility End</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Feasibility End</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Insurance Binding</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Insurance Binding</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Loan Commitment</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Loan Commitment</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Earnest Money Due</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Earnest Money Due</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Contract Executed</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Contract Executed</label>
            </value>
        </valueSetDefinition>
    </valueSet>
</CustomField>
